[00:12.74]Some people will use a symbolism
[00:15.86]of the relationship of
[00:16.90]God to the universe wherein
[00:19.26]God is a brilliant light
[00:23.38]only somehow veiled
[00:25.18]hiding underneath
[00:26.64]all these forms that you see as you look around you
[00:30.46]So far so good
[00:31.80]But the truth is funnier than that
[00:34.36]It is that you
[00:35.86]are looking right at the brilliant light now
[00:40.50]That the experience you are having
[00:42.51]which you call ordinary everyday consciousness
[00:45.42]pretending you're not it
[00:47.94]that experience is exactly the same thing as it
[00:51.84]There's no difference at all
[00:56.98]And when you find that out
[00:58.22]you'll laugh yourself silly
[01:01.60]That's the great discovery
[01:06.24]In other words, when you really start to see things
[01:10.46]and you look at an old paper cup
[01:14.16]and you go into the nature of what it is to see
[01:17.98]what vision is, or what smell is
[01:20.40]or what touch is
[01:21.90]you realize that that vision of the paper cup is the
[01:26.98]brilliant light of
[01:30.08]the cup
[01:34.06]Nothing could be brighter
